From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:23:43 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: macaudio: Cap every CS42L84 jack at the DAC's 0
 dB

The J616s/J713 jack was capped 6 dB below the DAC's 0 dB by a margin
chosen at bring-up; the other CS42L84 machines had no cap and reached
the DAC's digital gain above 0 dB, which only clips. macOS's own
headphone volume ends at 0 dB on every machine whose audio
configuration we have collected. Drop the per-board value and cap every
CS42L84 jack at 0 dB. Cards without a CS42L84 jack have no such
control and are left alone.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4d8d55ded153d98fa0cde5288fcf0680418173e2)

[j604 backport: omacom 7.2.11 has no J713 card (aurora 272a6ffe0e), so the context of its config field and match-table entries is absent here; this commit's own change (drop jack_max_vol, cap every CS42L84 jack at 0 dB) is unchanged. The J604 jack uses macaudio_j616_jack_cfg.]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c | 27 +++++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index fbf9a771cf..f5166e3f22 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -130,11 +130,6 @@ struct macaudio_platform_cfg {
 	 * keeps the other front-ends on their link numbers.
 	 */
 	unsigned int route_only_fes;
-	/*
-	 * The highest headphone volume, a "Jack DAC Playback Volume" value
-	 * (CS42L84_DAC_DB()), 0 for the codec's own maximum.
-	 */
-	int jack_max_vol;
 };
 
 static const char *volume_control_names[] = {
@@ -159,7 +154,6 @@ static const char *volume_control_names[] = {
 
 /* CS42L84 DAC: 0.5 dB steps from -128 dB, 256 = 0 dB, up to +12 dB */
 #define CS42L84_DAC_0DB 256
-#define CS42L84_DAC_DB(x) (CS42L84_DAC_0DB + 2 * (x))
 
 struct ma_codec_idle {
 	int idle_mode;
@@ -2010,10 +2004,18 @@ static int macaudio_fixup_controls(struct snd_soc_card *card)
 			 "Apple%s", p + 1);
 	}
 
-	/* Before the card registers: userspace never sees the codec's full range */
-	if (ma->cfg->jack_max_vol)
+	/*
+	 * Before the card registers, so userspace never sees the codec's full
+	 * range: a CS42L84 jack stops at the DAC's 0 dB. Above it the DAC only
+	 * adds digital gain, which clips a full-scale signal, and macOS's own
+	 * headphone volume ends at 0 dB on every machine (the "Built-in
+	 * Headphone" OutputVolumeMax of the machine's audio configuration).
+	 * The same for every board; a card without a CS42L84 jack (the
+	 * speaker-only cards) has no such control.
+	 */
+	if (snd_soc_card_get_kcontrol(card, "Jack DAC Playback Volume"))
 		CHECK(snd_soc_limit_volume, "Jack DAC Playback Volume",
-		      ma->cfg->jack_max_vol, 1);
+		      CS42L84_DAC_0DB, 1);
 
 	if (!ma->has_speakers)
 		return 0;
@@ -2431,13 +2433,6 @@ struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_j616_jack_cfg = {
 	.dai_fmt = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_DSP_A | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CBC_CFC | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_IB_NF,
 	.fe_cpu_is_platform = true,
 	.route_only_fes = BIT(1),
-	/*
-	 * Above 0 dB the DAC only adds digital gain, which clips a full-scale
-	 * signal. The 6 dB below that are margin: the analog full scale of
-	 * this board's headphone output is unmeasured, and macOS adapts it to
-	 * the impedance it detects, which this driver does not.
-	 */
-	.jack_max_vol = CS42L84_DAC_DB(-6),
 };
 
 struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_fallback_cfg = {
